        <body>
            <div xml:id="d707">

                <pb facs="0750" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg700"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                1, 1894</hi></date>. (Received October 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 316.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a note from the
                    Sublime Porte, of the 26th ultimo, announcing final action by the superior
                    provincial court in the case against the assailants of Miss Melton, and
                    requesting from me an expression of approval. I also transmit a copy of my
                    response, dated the 27th ultimo, expressing my approval of the energy displayed
                    by the Turkish Government in the prosecution.</p>
                <pb facs="0751" n="701" xml:id="pg701"/>
                <p>There is a discrepancy between the verbal statement of the grand vizier to me and
                    the note verbale, in that the latter omits the name of Taklio as one of the
                    convicted men. The note verbale was sent by Said Pasha. My telegram was based on
                    the verbal statement of the grand vizier.</p>
                <p>The fact that the state’s attorney has appealed from the judgment of acquittal,
                    as to five men found not guilty, you will note. I will personally inspect the
                    evidence when the record reaches here, and urge a conviction or consent to a
                    dismissal as the facts may seem to require.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>



